摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Tavily-powered optional search tool for DeepSeek Harness (rc.7 plugin management): multi-key rotation/failover, usage gauge, settings card in Plugins → configuration; the built-in web_search is never replaced. | DSH Tavily 可选高级搜索工具（rc.7 插件管理）：多 Key 轮换/故障转移、用量仪表盘、插件配置页设置卡片；内置 web_","id":"gh:1335099437","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-tavily","slug":"moguiyu/dsh-tavily","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-market","dsh-plugins","tavily","web-search"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Tavily-powered optional search tool for DeepSeek Harness (rc.7 plugin management): multi-key rotatio"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"n/failover, usage gauge, settings card in Plugins → configuration; the built-in web_search is never "},{"id":"p1s3","text":"replaced. | DSH Tavily 可选高级搜索工具（rc.7 插件管理）：多 Key 轮换/故障转移、用量仪表盘、插件配置页设置卡片；内置 web_"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-tavily"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"[](https://awesome-dsh-plugin.com/p/moguiyu/dsh-tavily--packages-dsh-tavily/) [](https://dshfind.com"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"/zh/plugins/moguiyu/dsh-tavily?ref=badge)"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Tavily web search for DeepSeek Harness (DSH) — **multiple API keys**, **rotation and failover**, a *"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"*live usage gauge**, the direct **`extract` / `map` / `crawl`** tools, **`research`** for synthesize"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"d reports, and a key-management card on the **Plugins** page."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"The built-in `web_search` tool is **never replaced**: Tavily is an *addition* to the native search, "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"not a swap-in for it. This plugin registers no web-search provider and never rewrites `web.searchPro"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"wap-in for it. This plugin registers no web-search provider and never rewrites `web.searchProvider`."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Highlights"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- 🔑 **Multiple Tavily API keys** — manage a flat key list from the DSH UI.\n- 🔁 **Key rotation & fail"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"over** — round-robin across keys; automatically retries on HTTP 401/429/432/433, and a load-balance "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"mode caps in-flight requests per Tavily account.\n- 📊 **Live usage gauge** — per-key Tavily usage and"},{"id":"p8s4","text":" totals, fetched server-side without exposing keys.\n- ⚡ **Direct Tavily tools** — `tavily_extract` r"},{"id":"p8s5","text":"eads a known URL's content, `tavily_map` discovers a site's links, and `tavily_crawl` pulls an entir"},{"id":"p8s6","text":"e site, all under the same key rotation.\n- 📝 **Research reports** — `tavily_research` runs Tavily's "},{"id":"p8s7","text":"Research endpoint (`mini`/`pro`/`auto`), waits for the task and returns a synthesized, cited report;"},{"id":"p8s8","text":" `tavily_get_research` collects one that was still running. Research costs far more credits than sea"},{"id":"p8s9","text":"rch (mini 4–110, pro 15–250), so it stays opt-in per call."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"### From the Plugins page"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"1. Open **Plugins** in the DSH sidebar and choose **Add plugin**.\n2. Enter the npm package name **`@"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"moguiyu/dsh-tavily`**, or the GitHub address\n**`https://github.com/moguiyu/dsh-tavily`** for the sou"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"rce. The field also takes a tarball or an\nabsolute local path.\n3. Press **Install**, then **Enable n"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"ow**. A freshly installed bundle stays switched **off** until\nyou enable it."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"The card then renders on the `dsh-tavily` bundle's own page — between its description and its rows."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### From the CLI"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The dialog accepts exactly what `dsh plugin add` accepts, so either route works:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"`--profile <name>` picks the profile to install into; both forms resolve to the same plugin."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"> **Requirements** — DSH is a development preview (`0.1.x-rc/alpha`, `0.2.x-rc/alpha`). The tools an"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"d the key/usage routes are **verified** on `0.1.6-alpha.2`, `0.1.7-rc.2`, `0.2.0-rc.2`, the `0.2.1-r"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"c` line and the `0.2.2-rc` line, and are **expected to work on every declared line back to `0.1.0-rc"},{"id":"p17s4","text":".7`** — the peer range is deliberately wider than the verified store matrix. Both the **card** and t"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"he **Plugins-page install route** need `0.1.6-alpha.2` or newer, the release that added the Plugins "},{"id":"p17s6","text":"page and moved plugin configuration there; on older lines the plugin is fully functional and install"},{"id":"p17s7","text":"s from the CLI, it simply has no card. The npm name is the scoped `@moguiyu/dsh-tavily`, not the sim"},{"id":"p17s8","text":"ilarly-named community `dsh-tavily` provider-swap plugin."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"> **Compatibility** — `0.3.x` is a single self-contained package: the tools, the routes and the card"},{"id":"p18s2","text":" all live in `@moguiyu/dsh-tavily`, which uses only the long-stable `ctx.tools` / `ctx.webServer` / "},{"id":"p18s3","text":"`ctx.credentials` / `ctx.systemPrompt` seams. There is no version-specific code path left to feature"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"-detect. Peer ranges list one comparator per host tuple (`^0.1.0-rc.7`, `^0.1.1-rc.1`, `^0.1.2-alpha"},{"id":"p18s5","text":".2`, `^0.1.3-alpha.1`, `^0.1.5-0`, `^0.1.6-0`, `^0.1.7-0`, `^0.2.0-0`, `^0.2.1-0`, `^0.2.2-0`), beca"},{"id":"p18s6","text":"use prerelease comparators never cascade — a new host line means a new comparator, not a widened old"},{"id":"p18s7","text":" one. `dsh.compatibility.dshReleases` is the narrower, actually-verified store matrix: a rolling win"},{"id":"p18s8","text":"dow over the last few host lines, not a historical ledger. Both are generated from one file, `compat"},{"id":"p18s9","text":"ibility.json`, so they cannot drift apart."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Packages"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"**One package.** Earlier releases also shipped `@moguiyu/dsh-tavily-backend` and `@moguiyu/dsh-tool-"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"tavily-search`. From `0.3.0` both are folded into `@moguiyu/dsh-tavily`, which is now self-contained"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"; the two old packages are deprecated and no longer updated."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Package | Role |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| `@moguiyu/dsh-tavily` | Everything: `tavily_search` + `tavily_extract` / `tavily_map` / `tavily_cr"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"awl` + `tavily_research` / `tavily_get_research`, the key/usage routes, and the Plugins-page card |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Credentials"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- `TAVILY_API_KEYS` — comma-separated key list; the tools rotate through it, retrying on HTTP 401/42"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"9.\n- `TAVILY_API_KEY` — primary key auto-synced to the first key."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Both are managed automatically by the card. Keys never leave the server unmasked, and no state file "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"tomatically by the card. Keys never leave the server unmasked, and no state file holds key material."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Key usage strategy"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- **Rotate each key** — round-robin; on HTTP 401/429/432/433 the next key is tried.\n- **Lowest usage"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" first / Highest usage first** — re-order keys by live Tavily usage on save.\n- **Load balance** — ke"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ep at most *N* requests in flight per Tavily account (1 by default) and spread concurrent calls acro"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"ss accounts, so one free account is never hit in parallel. Tavily's 100 requests/minute applies per "},{"id":"p27s5","text":"account, and several keys can share one account; the grouping is inferred from each key's `account` "},{"id":"p27s6","text":"block on `/usage`, and any key can be pinned or split off by hand in the card's **Account** column."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Keys that cannot serve a request are skipped rather than failing the call: **401, 429, 432 (plan\nlim"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"it) and 433 (pay-as-you-go limit) all fail over** to the next key, and every key is tried at most\non"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"(pay-as-you-go limit) all fail over** to the next key, and every key is tried at most\nonce per call."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Tavily tools"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"`tavily_search` plus the direct tools and the research pair, all independent of `web_search`:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
